       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.
           AKRUPDT.

      *AUTHOR.
      *
      *REMARKS.  THIS IS THE AKRON UPDATE PROGRAM.
      *
      *    IN APRIL, 1982, THIS PROGRAM WAS MODIFIED TO UPDATE THE
      *    KSAM FILE "USAGFIL".  TRANSACTIONS AFFECTED ARE 10 (CORP
      *    CODE ADD) AND 20 (CORP CODE DELETE).  THESE ADDS AND
      *    DELETES ARE DONE TO THE KSAM FILE AS WELL AS TO THE
      *    DATABASE. CIH.
      *
      *    JUNE 14, 1982, THE CORPORATE CODE EDIT CHECK WAS CHANGED TO
      *    ACCEPT CORPCODES WITH AN ALPHA FIRST CHARACTER.  ALSO,
      *    PRODUCTION DATE WAS ADDED TO THE RAW MATERIAL ERROR REPORT
      *    AND AUDIT TRAIL.  THESE TWO REPORTS WERE ALSO SENT DIRECTLY
      *    TO THE MIXING CENTER PRINTER (PRINTER 17) VIA JSPOOLER
      *    INSTEAD OF TO THE LINE PRINTER.     LSB.
      *
      *    OCTOBER 4, 1982, A NEW TRANSACTION (TC-99) WAS ADDED FOR
      *    RIM PLANT START-UP.  THE PURPOSE OF THIS TRANSACTION IS
      *    TO LOAD RIM PLANT QUANTITIES INTO RIM PLANT LOCATIONS
      *    WITHOUT EFFECTING 321A.  LSB.
      *
      *    DECEMBER 20, 1982, LOGIC WAS ADDED TO CORP CODE DELETE
      *    TO HANDLE THE POSSIBILITY THAT A REQUISITION(S) IS CONNECTED
      *    TO THE CODE BEING DELETED IF SO THEN THE ENTIRE
      *    REQUISITION(S) IS DELETED THIS CONSISTS OF 3 DATA SETS
      *    -- MREQ, DREQD, DREQITM. NOTE THE ENTIRE REQ IS DELETED
      *    NOT JUST THE DATA SET CONNECTED TO MSTORERM (DREQITM) WHEN
      *    THE CODE IS DELETED
      *         KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *    APRIL 11, 1983, REARRANGED RAW MATERIAL LOGIC SO THAT THE
      *    SPOOLER CALLS ARE ONLY EXECUTED WHEN 50 TRANSACTIONS ARE
      *    BEING PROCESSED.         LSB.
      *
      *    MAY 24, 1983, CHANGED LOGIC TO ACCEPT MORE THAN ONE GROUP
      *    OF RAW MATERIAL TRANSACTIONS AT A TIME.        LSB.
      *
      *    JUNE 20, 1983 FIXED LOGIC PROBLEM WITH ADDING AND UPDATING
      *                 DESC IN DDESC TC '30'
      *      KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *     AUG 10,1983  PUT IN PRINT LOGIC FOR ADD,CHG.DEL CORP CODES
      *     AND THEIR DESCRIPTIONS.
      *     AUG 10,1983  PUT IN PRINT LOGIC FOR ADD,CHG,DEL VENDOR CODES
      *     AND THEIR ADDRESSES.
      *     AUG 10,1983  PUT IN LOGIC TO BYPASS THE DELETE LOGIC FOR
      *     VENDORS. THIS RTN PRINTS THEN GETS OUT.
      *                                     ATL.
      *
      *     AUG 11,1983  ALTERED TC-99 LOGIC FOR GADSDEN ONHAND
      *     LOADING. THIS TC-99 IS FOR ANY ONE-TIME SHOT ACTION.
      *                                     ATL.
      *
      *     SEPT 8,1983  ADDED RAW-MATL HOLD FIELDS WITH INDIVIDUAL
      *     PLANTS CHARGE DATA IN THEIR OWN GROUP.  ONCE THE CONTROL
      *     RECORD IS READ, I MOVE THE GIVEN PLANTS HOLD FIELDS TO
      *     THE "MASTER" GROUP.  THEN THE ACTUAL ISSUE LOGIC NEED
      *     NOT BE CHANGED FOR INDIVIDUAL PLANTS.
      *                                     ATL.
      *
      *    SEPT 12, 1983, MODIFIED PROGRAM TO UPDATE REQFILE IN THE
      *    CHEMICAL ONHAND UPDATE ROUTINE.  THIS IS DONE BY CALLING
      *    THE SUBPROGRAM "TREQFILU" WHICH HANDLES ALL LOGIC AND
      *    DECISIONS TO UPDATE REQFILE.  CIH.
      *
      *    NOV 1, 1983, CHANGED PROGRAM TO CALL NEW VERSION OF "TREQFILU"
      *    WHICH IS NOW IN THE SL.  NOTE PGM MUST BE RUN WITH "LIB=P"
      *    PARAMETER.  CIH.
      *
      *    ON FEB 15, 1984, CHANGED PARAMETERS FOR CALL TO
      *    "TREQFILU".  THE ADDED FIELDS ARE "SAVE-RSRVD-BEFORE"
      *    AND "STR-RESERVED" (RESERVED QTY AFTER THE TRANSACTION).
      *    THIS IS BECAUSE THE REQFILE UPDATE SUBPROGRAM WILL NOW CREATE
      *    AUTO REQS ON THE BASIS OF AVAILABLE RATHER THAN ONHAND.
      *    HOWEVER IN THIS PGM, "STR-RESERVED" IS USED FOR BOTH
      *    RESERVED BEFORE AND RESERVED AFTER PARAMETERS, SINCE THIS
      *    QTY CANNOT CHANGE DURING THE TRANSACTION. (THIS PGM DOES
      *    NOT CHANGE RESERVED, AND THE CODE IS LOCKED DURING THE
      *    TRANSACTION).  CIH.
      *
      *    ON AUGUST 28, 1984, CHANGED THIS PGM TO ADD AND DELETE TO
      *    THE "MALTKEY" DATASET FOR RAW MATERIALS.  IF A RAW MATERIAL
      *    IS ADDED, DELETED, OR CHANGED THEN THE ALTERNATE KEY FOR
      *    THAT RAW MATERIAL IS ADDED, DELETED, OR CHANGED IN THE ALT
      *    KEY DATASET.  FOR MAJOR GROUP 26 (CHEMICALS), THE ALT KEY
      *    IS THE ADJECTIVE OF THE FIRST LINE OF DESCRIPTION (IE,
      *    261034    -  "ADAMAX").  FOR MAJOR GROUP 27 (FABRICS),
      *    THE ALT KEY IS SOMEWHERE IN THE 2CD LINE OF DESCRIPTION
      *    (IE FOR "GOODYEAR BASE CODE A1955" THE ALT KEY IS "A1955").
      *    THIS CHANGE IS ACCOMPLISHED BY CALLING 2 SUBPROGRAMS -
      *    "TALTKEY" DOES THE ADDING OR DELETING, AND "TDETCODE"
      *    FINDS THE ALT KEY FOR FABRICS.  CIH.
      *
      *    ON SEPT. 11, 1984, CHANGED THE PARAMETERS FOR THE CALL TO
      *    "TREQFILU".  ADDED THE "BASE" PARAMETER.  THIS IS BECAUSE
      *    "TREQFILU" WILL SOON BE MODIFIED TO UPDATE THE DATABASE
      *    RATHER THAN THE KSAM FILE "REQFILE".  CIH.
      *
      *    ON OCTOBER 26, 1984 - CHANGED RAW MATERIAL ISSUE LOGIC TO
      *    UPDATE MSTORERM FOR LIVE PLANTS ONLY.   LSB.
      *
      *    NOVEMBER 26, 1984 - MODIFIED EDIT LOGIC TO ALLOW ANY
      *    ALPHA-NUMERIC COMBINATION FOR A CORP CODE AS LONG AS THE
      *    FIRST POSITION IS NOT BLANK. THIS SIMPLY REMOVES THE
      *    RESTRICTION THAT NON-NUMERIC CODES BEGIN WITH A LETTER. CAK.
      *
      *    NOV 30, 1984 - CHANGE RAW BATCH REPORTS SO THEY ARE NOW
      *    WRITTEN TO MPE FILES AND PRINTED OFF USING THE PRINT
      *    REPORT PROGRAM (TPRTRPT) THIS WILL ENABLE PLANTS TO DIRECT
      *    1 OR MORE PRINTOUTS TO 1 OR MORE DIFFERENT PRINTERS WITHOUT
      *    CHANGING AKRON UPDATE.
      *              K MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *    ON APRIL 10, 1985, CHANGED THE PROGRAM TO UPDATE
      *    THE REQUISITION DATA SETS FOR INTERNATIONAL
      *    REQUISITIONS.  THESE INTERNATIONAL REQS WILL BE PASSED
      *    FROM THE MAINFRAME WITH A TRANSACTION CODE OF "88".
      *    A REPORT OF REQUISITION UPDATES WILL BE PRINTED BY USING
      *    THE PROGRAM "XPRTRPT" IN THE JOB STREAM - THE JOB WILL
      *    CHECK FOR THE JCW "REQRPTSW", WHICH WILL BE SET IF ANY
      *    "88" TCs ARE ENCOUNTERED.  IF SO, IT WILL PRINT THE REPORT
      *    OF REQ UPDATES. (THIS IS SIMILAR TO THE METHOD USED BY
      *    THE RAW BATCH REPORT LOGIC).  ALSO ADDED A CIRCULAR ERROR
      *    FILE "DAKRERR", WHICH WILL BE CREATED IF IT DOES NOT EXIST.
      *    THIS WILL HOLD ANY REQ UPDATE ERRORS.  IT CAN LATER BE
      *    EXPANDED TO HOLD ERRORS FOR ANY OTHER TRANSACTIONS.
      *    CIH.
      *
      *    ON MAY 6, 1985, CHANGED THE INTERNATIONAL REQ UPDATE LOGIC
      *    TO ALSO ADD AN "UNLINKED" (PO NUMBER, BUYER NUMBER ARE
      *    SPACES) "DREQD" SEGMENT ENTRY TO THE DATABASE UPON ADDING
      *    THE REQ.  THIS IS TO MAKE THE DATA CONSISTENT WITH THE WAY
      *    OTHER REQ PROGRAMS EXPECT IT.  CIH.
      *
      *    ON MAY 14, 1985, ADDED A NEW TRANSACTION TYPE "60".  THIS
      *    TRANS TYPE IS USED TO UPDATE INVOICE CHECK NUMBERS FROM THE
      *    MAINFRAME, BASED ON A KEY OF REGISTER NUMBER.  THE MAINFRAME
      *    PASSES REGISTER NUMBER, CHECK NUMBER, INVOICE NUMBER, CHECK
      *    DATE, ETC.  THE CHECK NUMBER AND CHECK DATE ARE THEN UPDATED
      *    ON THE HP INVOICING SYSTEM IN THE "DINVRCD" DATASET.  THIS
      *    NEW TRANSACTION IS HANDLED BY CALLING THE SUBROUTINE
      *    "TAKINVCK".  THE PURPOSE OF CALLING A SUBPROGRAM FOR NEW
      *    TRANSACTIONS IS TO AVOID INCREASING THE SIZE OF THIS
      *    MAIN PROGRAM FOR EACH TRANSACTION, AND TRY TO MAKE THE
      *    PROGRAM MORE MAINTAINABLE.  CIH.
      *
      *    SEPT. 10, 1985
      *        ADDED LAWTON IN AS A LIVE PLANT FOR BANBURY EXPLOSIONS.
      *           KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *
      *    SEPT. 16, 1985
      *       FIXED PROBLEM WITH VENDOR CODE ADDS WHEN THE VENDOR
      *       WAS USED ON A INVOICE WHICH CAUSED AN ENTRY IN
      *       'AVENDCODE' AND THIS PROGRAM USED AVENDCODE TO
      *       SEE IF THE VENDOR EXISTED. I CHANGED THIS EDIT TO
      *       LOOK AT THE 'DVENDOR' DATA SET.
      *          KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *    SEPT 19, 1985
      *       CHANGED THE BANBURY EXPLOSION LOGIC FOR LAWTON.  THE
      *       CHARGE DEPT, REQUESTING DEPT, AND EXPENSE CLASS FOR
      *       BANBURY EXPOSION ISSUES (TC 333) IS HARD-CODED INTO THE
      *       PROGRAM BY PLANT CODE.  ADDED THE CORRECT DATA FOR
      *       LAWTON.  CIH.
      *
      *     SEPT. 26, 1985
      *       TOOK LAWTON OUT AS A LIVE PLANT FOR BANBURY EXPLOSIONS.
      *          KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *    DEC. 2, 1985
      *        ADDED LAWTON IN AS A LIVE PLANT FOR BANBURY EXPLOSIONS.
      *           KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *    12/05/85
      *        FIXED A BUG IN INTERNATIONAL REQUISITION UPDATE
      *        (TC 88).  IF A "DBPUT" ERROR WAS ENCOUNTERED ON
      *        "DREQITM" (SAY, DATA SET FULL), A "DBUNLOCK" WAS NOT
      *        DONE AFTER THE ERROR MESSAGE, RESULTING IN ALL FOLLOWING
      *        DB CALLS ABORTING.  ADDED THE "DBUNLOCK" AFTER THE ERROR.
      *        CIH.
      *
      *    DEC 30, 1985
      *       1. ADDED A CHECK FOR COMPANY CODE COMPARING CO CODE IN
      *          RJECODES WITH CO. CODE IN MPLTINFO OF THE DATA BASE.
      *            KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *    03/27/86.
      *      TOOK OUT THE DELETE TRANSACTION FROM THIS PROGRAM.
      *      FROM NOW ON, ALL CORP CODES WILL BE DELETED BY A PROGRAM
      *      ON THE HP SIDE, AND A TRANSACTION PASSED UP TO THE IBM.
      *      THIS IS BECAUSE INVOICE DATA IS NOT STORED ON THE IBM,
      *      THUS THE IBM PROGRAM CANT KNOW WHEN ALLOW OR DISALLOW
      *      A CORPORATE CODE DELETION.  CIH.
      *
      *    MAY 8, 1986
      *      CHANGED INTERNATIONAL REQ. FILE FORMAT TO INCLUDE
      *      CO. CODE LIKE ALL OTHER FILE TYPES SO CO. CODE CHECK
      *      WILL WORK.
      *        KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *    05/12/86
      *      MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
      *      1.  CONVERTED TO CALL "TBLOWUP" IF FATAL ERROR IS
      *          ENCOUNTERED.
      *      2.  CHANGED TRANS 30 TO ADD THE NEW ENTRIES FOR DATA SETS
      *          "MKEYADJ", "DCODE", "DDESC2", "MMANUFACT", AND
      *          "DMANPART" AS REQUIRED.
      *          DESCRIPTION IS ADDED TO "DDESC" IF ENGLISH IS THE
      *          PRIMARY LANGUAGE, OTHERWISE IT IS ADDED TO "DDESC2".
      *          (DATA ON THE MAINFRAME IS ALWAYS ENGLISH, AND AT THE
      *          PLANT ENGLISH MUST BE EITHER THE PRIMARY OR SECONDARY
      *          LANGUAGE).
      *      3.  TOOK OUT THE DELETE VENDOR LOGIC SINCE IT ISN'T
      *          BEING USED.  IF IN THE FUTURE WE DECIDE TO ALLOW
      *          VENDOR DELETES FROM THE MAINFRAME, IT WOULD BE BETTER
      *          TO HAVE A SUBPROGRAM DO THE VENDOR DELETION.
      *          CIH.
      *
      *    06/04/86
      *      CHANGED MANUFACTURER LOGIC TO ALSO ADD THE MANUFACTURERS
      *      TO THE ENGLISH DESCRIPTION (DDESC OR DDESC2).  CIH.
      *
      *    06/13/86
      *      FIXED A BUG THAT SOMEHOW APPEARED IN THE INTERNATIONAL
      *      REQ LOGIC.  THE DATA WAS NO LONGER BEING PUT INTO THE
      *      "DREQNISIM" FIELDS, RESULTING IN "NULL ITEMS".  FIXED
      *      THIS.  CIH.
      *
      *   06/16/86.  C.I.HILLES.
      *     TOOK OUT THE ADD OF MANUFACTURERS TO DESCRIPTION.  THE SECOND
      *     BYTE OF MANUFACTER-PARTNO-TYPE IS NOW USED TO INDICATE WHETHER
      *     THAT MANUFACTURER HAS BEEN SELECTED BY THE USER TO SHOW UP ON
      *     DESCRIPTION DISPLAYS AND PRINTOUTS.  THIS DATA MUST BE RETAINED
      *     ON DOWNLOAD OF NEW MANUFACTURER INFO FROM MAINFRAME.  CHANGED
      *     PROGRAM TO RETAIN THIS DATA BY LOADING IT INTO A TABLE AS EACH
      *     MANUFACTURER IS DELETED - SO THE SELECTIONS BY MANUFACTURER CAN
      *     BE RETAINED UPON RE-ADD (IF THE MANUFACTURER STILL EXISTS).  CIH.
      *
      *    07/10/86.
      *    1.HAD TO ADD BACK CORP CODE DELETE LOGIC FOR KELLY PLANTS, SINCE
      *      ALL DELETES ARE HANDLED BY "PRAPS" IN CUMBERLAND, PASSED FROM
      *      CUMBERLAND TO AKRON, AND FROM THE AKRON MAINFRAME BACK DOWN TO THE
      *      PLANT THRU RJE.  THE DELETE WILL BE ALLOWED ONLY IF THE PLANT
      *      HAS THE "CDDL" KEY IN THE "MPLTINFO" DATASET.
      *
      *    2.CHANGED MANUFACTURER LOGIC.  CHANGED THE DEFAULT SELECTION
      *      OF A MANUFACTURER FOR A NEW CODE OR A NEW MANUFACTURER FOR AN OLD
      *      CODE.  IF A MANUFACTURER IS "SELECTED", IT WILL APPEAR ON THE
      *      CORP CODE DESCRIPTION ON PRINTOUTS AND DISPLAYS.  IF NOT SELECTED,
      *      IT WONT APPEAR.  THE OLD DEFAULT WAS TO SELECT THE MANUFACTURER
      *      ON A MANUFACTURER ADD FOR EITHER AN EXISTING CODE OR A NEW CODE.
      *      NOW, IF A NEW CODE IS ADDED THE SELECTION STILL DEFAULTS TO "B" -
      *      BOTH LANGUAGES.  BUT FOR AN ADD OF A MANUFACTURER FOR AN EXISTING
      *      CODE THE DEFAULT IS SPACES - NOT SELECTED.
      *      THE REASON FOR THIS CHANGE IS AS FOLLOWS:
      *         1.  DANVILLE CREATES CODE "BATTERY    FLASHLIGHT", AND HAS
      *             MANUFACTURER "EVERREADY".  THIS MANUFACTURER IS SELECTED AND
      *             WILL PRINT ON P.O.'S, STOREROOM WITHDRAWALS, ETC.
      *         2.  MALAYSIA LINKS TO THE SAME CODE, AND ADDS MANUFACTURER
      *             "HYOTOTA INCORPORATED".
      *         3.  THIS NEW LOGIC PREVENTS "HYOTOTA INCORPORATED" FROM NOW
      *             PRINTING ON DANVILLE'S DOCUMENTS.
      *
      *    AUG. 18, 1986
      *        1.  TOOK OUT THE EDIT CHECK FOR VENDOR CODES THAT
      *            REQUIRED THE VENDOR TO BE A 'PAYTO' VENDOR ONLY
      *                 KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *
      *    OCT. 12, 987.
      *        1.  ACCEPT VENDOR PHONE AND CONTACT (RECORD ID '09').
      *        2.  CUT A TC '100' FOR EVERY CODE ADD (AKRUPDT T/C 20).
      *                ANNETTE TREUDLER.
      *
